From 026b8f0cca2012f4794290a80026638669c89ac8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saurias92 <66642624+Aspis0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 11:15:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] session: disable mmap_prefetch when expert streaming is
 enabled

With --moe-stream, experts are read via O_DIRECT when needed and
--dense-weights anon copies the dense trunk out of the mmap. Prefaulting
the whole GGUF is I/O that will never be used (F4.8: 19.14 GiB page-fault
of 20.76 GiB load read_bytes on Qwen3.6-35B UD-IQ2_M).

Sets mparams.mmap_prefetch = false only when cfg.moe.enabled; non-streaming
loads keep the classic warm-load default (true). Depends on llama.cpp
kalsa/mmap-prefetch-opt (mmap_prefetch field).
---
 core/src/engine/session.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/src/engine/session.cpp b/core/src/engine/session.cpp
index 9fd5a06..cd88cc2 100644
--- a/core/src/engine/session.cpp
+++ b/core/src/engine/session.cpp
@@ -408,6 +408,13 @@ std::unique_ptr<Session> Session::open(const SessionConfig & cfg,
     mparams.use_mmap = true;
     mparams.use_extra_bufts = false;
     mparams.n_gpu_layers = 0;
+    // Streaming reads experts via O_DIRECT when needed, and --dense-weights anon copies the
+    // dense trunk out of the mmap; prefaulting the whole GGUF is I/O that will never be used
+    // (measured 19.14 GiB page-fault of 20.76 GiB load read_bytes on Qwen3.6-35B UD-IQ2_M).
+    // Leave mmap_prefetch=true for non-streaming loads (classic warm path).
+    if (cfg.moe.enabled) {
+        mparams.mmap_prefetch = false;
+    }
 
     // Optional active-expert override: reduce the model's top-k routing (e.g. 8 -> 6) to cut
     // per-token compute and — under streaming — flash I/O, at a quality cost. Applied purely
